SUMMARY:The Fall St. James Chamber Music Concert
DESCRIPTION:St James Episcopal Church is excited to announce that this coming Sunday November 15th at 4PM it will host a chamber music concert featuring the renowned violinist Naoko Tanaka\, along with 10 other esteemed musicians. Ms Tanaka will be performing “The Lark Ascending” by Ralph Vaughan Williams. \nAlso on the program are works by Bach\, Poulenc\, Persichetti\, Beethoven and Dvorak. \nNaoko Tanaka has given concert tours as a soloist and chamber musician in the U.S.\, South America\, Europe\, Asia and Canada. A former member of The Theater Chamber Players of The Kennedy Center and The Orpheus Chamber Orchestra\, she is a current member of the New York Philomusica and serves as concert master of St Luke’s Chamber Ensemble. She is on the faculty at the Juilliard School\, Brooklyn College Conservatory of Music\, and The Aspen Music School during the summer. She has recorded for Deutsche Gramophone\, Columbia Records\, and Music Masters.\nSt James Episcopal Church is at 581 Valley Road in Upper Montclair. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
