SUMMARY:The LGBTQ+ Sewing Club
DESCRIPTION:Do you wish your clothes matched your gender and body type better? Does your wardrobe need an update? Join the LGBTQ+ Sewing Club! Learn basic sewing skills and update your clothes to match your identity and style. Not only is learning to sew a great life skill to have\, but you will also be able to upcycle and restyle thrifted clothes and hand-me-downs. No prior sewing experience necessary! \nBring a piece of clothing that you would like to upcycle. If you have a sewing machine or sewing needles and materials from home you want to use you are welcome to bring in and use during this session. You are also welcome to use a sewing machine in the studio. Allies are also welcome to join. \nA portion of the proceeds will be donated to Out Montclair. Visit https://outmontclair.org/ to learn more about their mission. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
